        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-repetition-timing-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Distinguish repetition and timing expectations",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "又 presents an actual recurrence; 再 requests or anticipates a later repetition. 就 and 才 depend on a reference expectation: 就 can mark an early, immediate or easy event, while 才 can mark only then or later than expected. They do not have one fixed English translation.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他又来了。",
                "pinyin": "tā yòu lái le 。",
                "meaning": "He has come again.",
                "audio": "0077e332d7240fc4a5c7d177076623da5badf597a984f403c8568fe452a4ffc1"
              },
              {
                "text": "请明天再来。",
                "pinyin": "qǐng míngtiān zài lái 。",
                "meaning": "Please come again tomorrow.",
                "audio": "ba0e7d4d45469ed4de37a5c32ac5f6e4fa511008c546c039ea887d3a9ee9922d"
              },
              {
                "text": "他八点就来了。",
                "pinyin": "tā bā diǎn jiù lái le 。",
                "meaning": "He came as early as eight.",
                "audio": "668b55b1ed675a52441963e2de071ddcbd6bb9d3a0413251c167716aabf63fdf"
              },
              {
                "text": "他九点才来。",
                "pinyin": "tā jiǔ diǎn cái lái 。",
                "meaning": "He did not come until nine.",
                "audio": "93cc0ca1875ece7174c773be5d6b974624f12e9839b9acc0053eb8a0da768df5"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
